course: dictionary
lesson: 13304
title: Gray and its many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Gray (grey in the UK) is a good example. Most of the time it is a colour, the shade between black and white. «The sky was gray all day and the rain would not stop.» The clues are sky and rain, so gray means dull and cloudy.
explain: Gray can also describe a feeling. «Their gray mood matched the weather.» Nobody is painting anything here. A gray mood is dull and gloomy. Ask yourself: is the writer talking about something you can see, or about how someone feels?
explain: Gray can be a verb too. «Grandma's hair started to gray with age.» Here gray means to turn gray, the way hair changes colour as people grow older. It is the same word, but it does a different job in the sentence.
explain: Sometimes gray is part of a phrase. «It was a gray area, so nobody knew who was right.» A gray area is something not clearly right or wrong. Swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Gray is the colour between black and white, like ash or rain clouds.
fact: In the UK the spelling is grey, but the meaning is the same.
fact: In art, gray is made by mixing black and white.
fact: To gray, as a verb, means to turn gray with age, and it is used mostly about hair.
fact: «Gray matter» is a phrase that means the brain.
exercise: «The sky was gray all day and the rain would not stop.» What colour is the sky? | Bright yellow | *Gray | Black | Green
exercise: «Their gray mood matched the weather.» What does gray mean here? | Very hot | *Dull and gloomy | Bright and cheerful | A shade of blue
exercise: «It was a gray area, so nobody knew who was right.» What is a gray area? | A park full of trees | *Something not clearly right or wrong | A shade of green paint | Something bright and shiny
test: «Grandma's hair started to gray with age.» In this sentence, gray is a verb. What does it mean? | To paint something red | *To turn gray, as hair does with age | To shout very loudly
test: In art class, how do you make gray? | Mix red and yellow | Mix blue and green | Mix orange and pink | *Mix black and white
exam: In the sentence «Gray matter helps you think», what does gray matter mean? | A pile of grey dust | A soft grey rock | A type of cloud | *The brain
